					"declarations": [
						"Test",
						"each",
						"prop"
					]
				},
				{
					"package": "vitest",
					"declarations": [
						"TestCollectorCallable",
						"EachFunctionReturn",
						"TestForFunctionReturn"
					]
				}
			],
			"searches": [
				{
					"module": "packages/testing/src/explore.ts",
					"names": [
						"explore",
						"exhaust"
					]
				},
				{
					"module": "packages/testing/src/interleave.ts",
					"names": [
						"interleave"
					]
				}
			],
			"scaffolds": [
				{
					"module": "test/support/schedules/runner.ts",
					"names": [
						"runSchedule"
					],
					"reason": "It compiles a hand-written schedule into the concurrency driver's script strategy, so every hand schedule reaches the library's interleave without searching an order; a case that runs one is a search only when it calls explore, exhaust or interleave over the schedules itself."
				}
			],
			"exempt": [
				{
					"files": [
						"test/types/examples/blocks.test.ts",
						"test/types/examples/examples.test.ts"
					],
					"reason": "The README's and SKILL.md's mirror: blocks.test.ts holds every documented block to its mirrored fixture, and examples.test.ts typechecks those fixtures and fails each refusal the README states with exactly the diagnostic it names, so the documentation is checked code; its blocks are the documentation, never inputs a person chose to test."
				},
				{
					"files": [
						"test/unit/dev/package.test.ts"
					],
					"reason": "The published-package gate: the README's and SKILL.md's mirrored programs, the one sanctioned example code, typecheck against the declarations the build emits alone, so those declarations are self-contained and never any; its other case exhausts the published entry points and bins against the source."
				},
				{
					"files": [
						"packages/testing/src/engine.bench.ts"
					],
					"reason": "The testing library's engine bench: it measures what generating, replaying, enumerating, shrinking and exploring cost, a performance measure, never a verdict a person wrote."
				},
				{
					"files": [
						"test/pg/bench/"
					],
					"reason": "The performance gates: each measures a workload against its gate, a performance property, never a verdict a person wrote."
				},
				{
					"files": [
						"test/types/api/access.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/config.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/handle.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/recursion.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/surface.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/untyped.test.ts",
						"test/types/api/workload.test.ts",
						"test/types/changeset/changeset.test.ts",
						"test/types/changeset/entry-owner.test.ts",
						"test/types/changeset/nesting.test.ts",
						"test/types/compute/compute.test.ts",
						"test/types/evidence/agreement.test.ts",
						"test/types/evidence/attachments.test.ts",
						"test/types/evidence/parameter.test.ts",
						"test/types/harness/harness.test.ts",
						"test/types/regex/agreement.test.ts",
						"test/types/schema/agreement.test.ts",
						"test/types/schema/generic.test.ts",
						"test/types/text/bytes.test.ts",
						"test/types/text/regex.test.ts"
					],
					"reason": "The type batch's population runners: the population is drawn by the testing library's generators, or exhausts a box the source's own rosters define, and is printed as one program the batch typechecks at once, so no case can run a search per program; each case checks the drawn population against the engine as oracle, or that its floor's witnesses reach every requirement."
				},
				{
					"files": [
						"test/types/query/budget/invariance.test.ts",
						"test/types/query/budget/scaling.test.ts",
						"test/types/regex/scaling.test.ts",
						"test/types/schema/budget/families.test.ts",
						"test/types/schema/budget/invariance.test.ts",
						"test/types/schema/budget/scaling.test.ts",
						"test/types/skeleton/budget/invariance.test.ts"
					],
					"reason": "The type layer's cost gates: each typechecks programs generated at three sizes an equal step apart and holds their types and instantiations to grow no faster than linearly, the second step adding no more than the first (test/support/growth.ts), a performance property; or holds the largest program's inference and refusals to its twin's, the same declarations at the smallest scale its probes read. No verdict is one a person wrote."
				}
			]
		},
